<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010), Lefebvre et al. (2023) & Brauns et al. (2024) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow, curved-surface active nematic myosin mechanics & cell intercalation (Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8))",
        "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010), Lefebvre et al. (2023) & Brauns et al. (2024) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow, curved-surface active nematic myosin mechanics & cell intercalation faithfully reproduces Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A predictive (uncalibrated) flow-correlation against measured PIV fields, two-way vertex-continuum coupling, 3D yolk/vitelline fluid-structure interaction, or digitised values for the Bertet/Blankenship/Brauns anchors (verified_offline = false)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz compressible Stokes-Brinkman solver on the 500x420 um cartographic domain (Green's function L2 error 3.6e-16), 6-regime wild-type/mutant benchmark and 30 min Lagrangian marker advection (unchanged from Pass 2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: 56x48 (s, phi) finite-difference solver of the same force balance ON the prolate spheroid a = 250, b = 105 um using the exact embedded covariant strain, metric and Gaussian curvature K = a^2/g_ss^2 (sphere-limit analytic residual 5.8e-3, order 2.04; curved-vs-cartographic WT vector correlation r = 0.833; 31% of nodes carry intrinsic pole-return flow), strain-rate positive-feedback myosin recruitment to its fixed point (g = 0.358, m*/m_0 = 1.70), and a 240-junction T1/rosette ledger with tension-isogonal split (125 collapses, 24 rosettes up to 10 cells, median shrink 7.75 min, intercalation share 0.64)",
        "reported_in_source: Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi); Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric/mechanical control of Myosin-II orientation and recruitment on the ellipsoidal embryo; Brauns et al. (2024) eLife 13:RP95521 tension-isogonal decomposition of convergent extension into cell rearrangement (T1/rosette) and cell-shape parts; Bertet et al. (2004) / Blankenship et al. (2006) junction shrinkage and 5-11-cell rosettes",
        "reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity",
        "transfer_boundary: Reduced curved-surface continuum: finite differences (not FEM) on a truncated (s, phi) grid with 20 um pole caps held at v = 0, single velocity-scale calibration to the 6.40 um/min WT peak, one-way myosin -> flow -> junction coupling; ledger rate constants calibrated to the Bertet (5-10 min) and Brauns (0.5-0.8) windows" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Polygonal Packing & Furrows" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Shape Index p_0* = 3.813" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py; output: docs/media/global_morphogenetic_flow_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/f18e3533; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782; artifact_sha256: c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg=2d7fad8f57edcadf..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/global_morphogenetic_flow_reference.json=160ead86ff9c447b..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/scout_manifest.json=990f3ea83019f3d1...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity | Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi); Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric/mechanical control of Myosin-II orientation and recruitment on the ellipsoidal embryo; Brauns et al. (2024) eLife 13:RP95521 tension-isogonal decomposition of convergent extension into cell rearrangement (T1/rosette) and cell-shape parts; Bertet et al. (2004) / Blankenship et al. (2006) junction shrinkage and 5-11-cell rosettes; reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz compressible Stokes-Brinkman solver on the 500x420 um cartographic domain (Green's function L2 error 3.6e-16), 6-regime wild-type/mutant benchmark and 30 min Lagrangian marker advection (unchanged from Pass 2) | Pass 3: 56x48 (s, phi) finite-difference solver of the same force balance ON the prolate spheroid a = 250, b = 105 um using the exact embedded covariant strain, metric and Gaussian curvature K = a^2/g_ss^2 (sphere-limit analytic residual 5.8e-3, order 2.04; curved-vs-cartographic WT vector correlation r = 0.833; 31% of nodes carry intrinsic pole-return flow), strain-rate positive-feedback myosin recruitment to its fixed point (g = 0.358, m*/m_0 = 1.70), and a 240-junction T1/rosette ledger with tension-isogonal split (125 collapses, 24 rosettes up to 10 cells, median shrink 7.75 min, intercalation share 0.64) | Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383); transfer_boundary: Reduced curved-surface continuum: finite differences (not FEM) on a truncated (s, phi) grid with 20 um pole caps held at v = 0, single velocity-scale calibration to the 6.40 um/min WT peak, one-way myosin -> flow -> junction coupling; ledger rate constants calibrated to the Bertet (5-10 min) and Brauns (0.5-0.8) windows; does_not_claim: A predictive (uncalibrated) flow-correlation against measured PIV fields, two-way vertex-continuum coupling, 3D yolk/vitelline fluid-structure interaction, or digitised values for the Bertet/Blankenship/Brauns anchors (verified_offline = false)]" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2006.09.007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02590>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09376>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.27454>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.78787>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.95521> ;
    pk1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-11>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-3>,
