<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010), Lefebvre et al. (2023) & Brauns et al. (2024) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow, curved-surface active nematic myosin mechanics & cell intercalation — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Gains: the Pass 3 curved-surface solver implements the actual covariant force balance on the prolate spheroid with exact metric and curvature (L523-L697), passes a second-order sphere-limit analytic check (L699-L739; residual 5.8e-3, order 2.04, energy ratio 0.9957), and shows the closed surface producing the return flow that the Pass 2 model injected by hand; strain-rate positive feedback (L757-L838) and the T1 ledger (L883-L995) add the Lefebvre-2023 and Brauns-2024 mechanisms, all backed by 6 machine-checked Lean theorems. Losses: the 6-regime benchmark still runs on the flat pipeline with the ad hoc pole-return term (L404-L416) and a phenomenological target-velocity formula (L422-L431) that the curved solver only reproduces at r = 0.833; the surface solver uses one-sided finite differences at 20 um pole caps held at v = 0 rather than a closed-surface FEM. Net -1." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py L404–L431: Flat 6-regime pipeline still adds an ad hoc pole-return circulation and rescales to a phenomenological target v_AP; curved solver not used for the regimes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py#L404-L431>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010), Lefebvre et al. (2023) & Brauns et al. (2024) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow, curved-surface active nematic myosin mechanics & cell intercalation — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "11 reference-anchored measurements (L1234-L1423) now include the sphere-limit residual (5.8e-3 vs 0), feedback amplification (1.70 vs local fixed point 1.56), intercalation share (0.64 vs Brauns ~0.65) and median shrink time (7.75 vs 7.5 min). Down 7 because (i) the wild-type \"flow correlation r = 0.924\" and the 6-regime r = 1.000 are constructed by projecting the WT field onto a synthetic observed direction built from the empirical r itself (L1046-L1055), so they validate nothing; (ii) the ledger's k_shrink/m_half/Hill-n were tuned to land inside the Bertet and Brauns windows (stated in the JSON note), so those two measurements are calibrations; (iii) the tension-isogonal split shows lambda_shape < 1 during the first ~10 min (Panel F), an inconsistency of the one-way coupling; (iv) the Bertet/Blankenship/Brauns anchors are flagged verified_offline = false." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py L1046–L1055: flow_correlation_r is synthesised from the empirical r (obs_unit built from emp_r), not computed against observed PIV data <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py#L1046-L1055>",
        "datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/intercalation_reference.json L89–L107: Ledger parameters note states k_shrink/m_half/n were calibrated to the Bertet and Brauns windows <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/intercalation_reference.json#L89-L107>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-measurement-6-regime-peak-ap-velocity-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-measurement-bcd-nos-tsl-maternal-ap-null-triple-mutant-peak-ap-velocity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-measurement-curved-surface-stokes-brinkman-sphere-limit-analytic-residual>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-measurement-isotropic-only-myosin-assumption-flow-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-measurement-median-dv-junction-shrink-time-to-t1>,
